# Build output
#
# One entry per command in command/, because `go build ./command/<name>` drops the binary at the repo root
# by default. A command whose binary is not listed here shows up as a large untracked file, and the
# next `git add -A` commits a platform-specific executable into history. Add a line when you add a
# command; `for c in command/*; do grep -q "^/$(basename $c)$" .gitignore; done` says which are missing.
#
# tools/ needs the same treatment and did not have it: `go build ./tools/<name>` lands at the root
# identically, and a 9 MB `vendor_react_fixtures` sat untracked here until a `git status` caught it.
# The check above only walks command/, so it reports clean while a tools/ binary is staged and waiting.
/formatdiff
/verify
/verify-differential
/verify-dispatch
/verify-release
/vendor_react_fixtures
/extract_oxc_fixtures
/generate_shims
/generate_collapse
/stage_dispatcher
/dist/

# Local caches — the graph snapshot and the rebuild cache both live here
/.cache/

# Operating systems and editors
#
# These are the only entries carried over from the ahra tree's ignore file. The rest of it covers a
# TypeScript application — node_modules, .next, .env, wrangler, a Python venv — and none of that can
# appear in a Go repository, so copying it whole would leave a reader guessing which lines are load
# bearing and which are inherited.
#
# .DS_Store is here because Finder writes one into any directory it displays, and two appeared at
# the root and under internal/ while this repository was being read rather than edited.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.localized
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.idea/

# Stray logs
#
# Nothing here writes a .log on purpose. The entry exists because a long command redirected to a
# file at the repository root is the ordinary way to read output that a pipe would truncate, and
# that file should never reach a commit.
*.log
